From: Jcode <noreply@jcode.local>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 01:44:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix stale layout after terminal resize

tdf computes its page layout from `Terminal::get_frame()` before calling
`Terminal::draw()`. Ratatui's `draw()` autoresizes the terminal before it
hands the `Frame` to the render closure, so a resize event can observe the
previous frame size here. That leaves the old page clipped after a shrink until
some later input causes another loop iteration.

Explicitly autoresize before reading the cached frame. This keeps the layout
calculation, `RenderNotif::Area`, and the following draw on the same terminal
size.
---
 src/main.rs | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/main.rs b/src/main.rs
--- a/src/main.rs
+++ b/src/main.rs
@@ -421,6 +421,11 @@ async fn enter_redraw_loop(
 			},
 		};
 
+		// `draw` autoresizes ratatui before handing the new Frame to the render
+		// closure. Keep the cached Frame in sync before reading it here, otherwise
+		// resize handling computes layout from the previous terminal size and the
+		// converted page remains clipped until the next input event.
+		term.autoresize()?;
 		let new_area = Tui::main_layout(&term.get_frame(), fullscreen);
 		if new_area != main_area {
 			main_area = new_area;
-- 
